  "label": "child is the one who is excited about not having to pick up the cotton candy and can eat it",
  "description": "The text 'you mean i don't have to pick it and i can eat it?!' is directly projected onto the visual of the child. The child's expression of innocent excitement and the gesture of raising a hand are mapped to the textual content, which represents the child's internal monologue or reaction. The child is the entity being mapped from the text, and the visual of the child is the entity being mapped to. This is a classic analogical mapping where the visual subject (the child) is identified as the speaker or experiencer of the text's message.",
